            "heading": "",
            "text": "EEE students get the best return from job oriented courses when they pick one area, such as power systems, control and PLC, embedded systems, electric vehicles or solar, and prove it with a safe, reviewed project rather than a certificate."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Choose one electrical area by reading live notices, learn its tools through free material first and finish one project that an engineer reviews."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "What sets EEE apart: Electrical work carries shock and fire risk, so employers weigh safety habits and standards awareness as heavily as software skill."
